{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgvp3sSBWbgoy8VAe5KgK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The next step is to confirm the link. Here is what happens after that:\n\n1. **Link.** The 12 FASTQ files are symlinked into `00_data/rnaseq_bulk/raw/`. Nothing is copied or moved. `RUNSHEET.txt` stays excluded.\n2. **Finalize.** This writes `files.csv` (read-only), `samples.csv` (with the six sample IDs and blank design columns), the project's `CONTEXT.md` and `HISTORY.md`. It also runs a `quick` integrity check: each link resolves, each file is non-empty and has the gzip header. A full decompression check is offered in stage 01, so it only runs on the samples you actually analyse.\n3. **Your turn.** Check the sample IDs in `samples.csv`. This is the cheapest point to catch a wrongly derived ID. Then fill in `condition`, `group` and `replicate` for each sample, and delete the rows of any sample you don't want analysed. The raw data stays linked, so you can undo that.\n4. **Stage 01.** It checks the design and writes the samplesheets. Later, stage 02 will ask you to pick the genome and the contrast from menus. Nothing scientific is guessed for you.\n\nBefore confirming, check that the six samples A1–A3 and B1–B3, as paired-end data, are the cohort you expect. Only you can tell whether these are the right files.\n\nConfirm to create symlinks under `00_data/rnaseq_bulk/raw/`, or provide a different path."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":560,"cache_read_input_tokens":36331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":560},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d468ab21-921a-5960-a6a1-f84f0ef5d7a2","uuid":"25008a89-67e